    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12443289/comment/12790314",
          "id": "12790314",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Did I miss you exploiting 'atomicity' of IW flags? For what I see you could declare them volatile with same result and less characters typed.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2009-12-14T19:53:18.492+0000",
          "updated": "2009-12-14T19:53:18.492+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12443289/comment/12790329",
          "id": "12790329",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "You're right!  AtomicBoolean is overkill...\n\nHmm, I think even volatile is overkill -- ensureOpen is only on a \"best effort\" basis; it makes no guarantee that it will be \"immediate\".  So I'll revert the changes to IndexWriter and remove the \"synchronized\" from ensureOpen.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2009-12-14T20:22:47.143+0000",
          "updated": "2009-12-14T20:22:47.143+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12443289/comment/12790352",
          "id": "12790352",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "New patch.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2009-12-14T20:31:42.578+0000",
          "updated": "2009-12-14T20:31:42.578+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12443289/comment/12790354",
          "id": "12790354",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "bq. ensureOpen is only on a \"best effort\" basis; it makes no guarantee that it will be \"immediate\"\nEhm. If you're okay with the possible case of ensureOpen()-guarded code to fail in grotesque ways because IW was in fact closed, but your \"best effort\" failed - why not drop ensureOpen() completely? It no longer \"ensures\" anything, what is its purporse?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
